{"page":178,"blocks":[{"x":0.04858,"y":0.05216,"w":0.20386,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"164 Chapter 3: Derivatives"},{"x":0.35368,"y":0.10707,"w":0.53248,"h":0.04417,"fs":0.01279,"n":4,"k":1,"t":"THEOREM 2—The Chain Rule If ƒ(u) is differentiable at the point u = g(x) and g(x) is differentiable at x, then the composite function (ƒ ∘g)(x) = ƒ(g(x)) is differentiable at x, and"},{"x":0.52475,"y":0.15247,"w":0.18625,"h":0.02238,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"(ƒ ∘g)′(x) = ƒ′(g(x)) # g′(x)."},{"x":0.35368,"y":0.18381,"w":0.34813,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"In Leibniz’s notation, if y = ƒ(u) and u = g(x), then"},{"x":0.5732,"y":0.20462,"w":0.05581,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = dy"},{"x":0.61311,"y":0.20529,"w":0.04374,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"du # du"},{"x":0.64097,"y":0.21429,"w":0.02167,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx,"},{"x":0.35367,"y":0.2443,"w":0.25097,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"where dy>du is evaluated at u = g(x)."},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.30556,"w":0.28452,"h":0.01311,"fs":0.01311,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"A Proof of One Case of the Chain Rule:"},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.32884,"w":0.37719,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Let ∆u be the change in u when x changes by ∆x, so that"},{"x":0.53362,"y":0.35186,"w":0.16935,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆u = g(x + ∆x) - g(x)."},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.37554,"w":0.24897,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Then the corresponding change in y is"},{"x":0.53268,"y":0.3979,"w":0.17125,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆y = ƒ(u + ∆u) - ƒ(u)."},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.42092,"w":0.3947,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"If ∆u ≠0, we can write the fraction ∆y>∆x as the product"},{"x":0.57034,"y":0.44106,"w":0.06372,"h":0.03089,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆y ∆x = ∆y"},{"x":0.6146,"y":0.4424,"w":0.05165,"h":0.03016,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆u # ∆u"},{"x":0.64678,"y":0.4514,"w":0.26556,"h":0.02055,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"∆x (1)"},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.48045,"w":0.19349,"h":0.01443,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"and take the limit as ∆x S 0:"},{"x":0.52991,"y":0.50411,"w":0.01903,"h":0.03089,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆y ∆x"},{"x":0.45518,"y":0.50478,"w":0.06661,"h":0.02973,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"dy dx = lim"},{"x":0.49518,"y":0.52419,"w":0.03171,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆xS0"},{"x":0.52991,"y":0.54094,"w":0.05165,"h":0.0315,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆y ∆u # ∆u"},{"x":0.47802,"y":0.5506,"w":0.04378,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.56209,"y":0.55838,"w":0.01898,"h":0.01346,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆x"},{"x":0.49518,"y":0.56102,"w":0.03171,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆xS0"},{"x":0.52991,"y":0.57778,"w":0.05765,"h":0.0315,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆y ∆u # lim"},{"x":0.59567,"y":0.58023,"w":0.01989,"h":0.02843,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆u ∆x"},{"x":0.47802,"y":0.58743,"w":0.04378,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.49518,"y":0.59785,"w":0.03171,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆xS0"},{"x":0.56093,"y":0.59785,"w":0.03171,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆xS0"},{"x":0.53054,"y":0.61461,"w":0.05765,"h":0.0315,"fs":0.01918,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆y ∆u # lim"},{"x":0.64897,"y":0.61624,"w":0.16073,"h":0.02433,"fs":0.01023,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"(Note that ∆u S 0 as ∆x S 0 since g is continuous.)"},{"x":0.5963,"y":0.61706,"w":0.01989,"h":0.02843,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"∆u ∆x"},{"x":0.47802,"y":0.62426,"w":0.0441,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= lim"},{"x":0.49518,"y":0.63469,"w":0.03234,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆uS0"},{"x":0.56156,"y":0.63469,"w":0.03171,"h":0.01039,"fs":0.00895,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"∆xS0"},{"x":0.47802,"y":0.65211,"w":0.03297,"h":0.02244,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"= dy"},{"x":0.49509,"y":0.65278,"w":0.04374,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"du # du"},{"x":0.52296,"y":0.66178,"w":0.02167,"h":0.02006,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx."},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.69245,"w":0.593,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The problem with this argument is that if the function g(x) oscillates rapidly near x, then"},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.70714,"w":0.59303,"h":0.04417,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"∆u can be zero even when ∆x ≠0, so the cancelation of ∆u in Equation (1) would be invalid. A complete proof requires a different approach that avoids this problem, and we give one such proof in Section 3.11."},{"x":0.32341,"y":0.78285,"w":0.58813,"h":0.02984,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 2 An object moves along the x-axis so that its position at any time t Ú 0 is given by x(t) = cos(t2 + 1). Find the velocity of the object as a function of t."},{"x":0.3234,"y":0.82607,"w":0.59309,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":1,"t":"Solution We know that the velocity is dx>dt. In this instance, x is a composite function: x = cos(u) and u = t2 + 1. We have"},{"x":0.54146,"y":0.86469,"w":0.18233,"h":0.02727,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"dx du = -sin(u) x = cos(u)"},{"x":0.54036,"y":0.8996,"w":0.01634,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"du"},{"x":0.5422,"y":0.9046,"w":0.18267,"h":0.02228,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"dt = 2t. u = t2 + 1"}]}